#==============================================================================================
#
#   block_formatting_context_2 - Layout::BlockFormattingContext: widths of block-level and
#                                floating boxes, used heights and inline children
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of LibWeb/Layout/BlockFormattingContext.cpp (lines 185-644): the width of
#       block-level boxes in normal flow (CSS 2.2 §10.3.3, with min-/max-width), avoiding float
#       intrusions, the shrink-to-fit width of floats (§10.3.5), block-level replaced widths
#       (§10.3.4), used heights when the height is or is not treated as auto (with the html and
#       body quirks), and the layout of a block container's inline children by an
#       InlineFormattingContext. The C++ lambdas of compute_width share their state through
#       LayoutBlockWidthSolver.
